					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/varian" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1424343); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1424343&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609233409" alt="Varian" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1424343)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/varian" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1424343); return false;" >Varian</a></span> <span class="odate time_1349623519 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Oct 2012 15:25</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1582753">
									

<p>It changes according to the most immediate threat. 90% of the time, it'll show when you're supposed to die of natural causes. But if you get into your car drunk and start driving it might change to show that day if you're going to be in a fatal crash. Or if you get cancer, it might change to show a few months or years.</p>
<p>And yes, there was a real appointment, but (in my thinking) Marshall quietly shuffled it along so he could do his thing.</p>
<p>EDIT: Forgot to mention, the watch was actually a sandbox idea I wrote that never got to the mainlist. It just didn't have that&#8230; Something. So I thought, &quot;Put that shit in prose! It'll be awesome!&quot;</p>

							</div>

								
